Back off and give up when no network backend is available.

ashell's network service retries a failed backend connection every five seconds
for the lifetime of the session, with no backoff and no give-up. On a host
without NetworkManager or iwd (ninja runs systemd-networkd) that is a permanent
loop, roughly 17k pointless D-Bus round trips a day.

This threads an attempt counter through the state machine, doubles the delay on
each failure, and moves to a new `Disabled` state after six attempts, on the
grounds that a system with no supported backend will not grow one mid-session.

Still needed as of 0.10.0: upstream continues to hardcode
`error!("Network service error, retrying in 5 seconds")` with a flat five second
sleep and an unconditional return to `State::Init`.

Refreshed for 0.10.0, which added a third field to `State::Active` and so broke
the first hunk's context.

Recheck against src/services/network/mod.rs on every ashell bump.

